# Line-ending policy — study 04 (configuration portal)
#
# A generated report carries an "inputs digest": a content hash over the bytes of every
# result file in the run. Git's line-ending conversion rewrites those bytes on checkout,
# so the same measurements hash differently after a clone, a new worktree or a branch
# switch. That is not hypothetical here: the repository's own study 03 matrix hashed two
# different ways, and the fix was to pin the affected trees to LF.
#
# This file is deliberately scoped to study 04. The root .gitattributes covers studies 02
# and 03 and study 01 pins its own tree; a study-scoped file keeps this study's merge
# surface small while the repository is being worked on by more than one agent.
#
# Result JSON and generated reports are the files whose bytes a digest depends on, so they
# are the ones that must never be converted. Shell, Go and SQL files are pinned too: this
# repository is edited from Windows, where an unset core.autocrlf plus CRLF on disk already
# produces a whole checkout of phantom modifications, and that is a trap worth not adding
# to.

# Provenance: these bytes are hashed, so they are pinned.
results/**           text eol=lf
reports/**           text eol=lf

# Everything executable or readable as documentation.
*.sh                 text eol=lf
*.go                 text eol=lf
*.sql                text eol=lf
*.md                 text eol=lf
*.puml               text eol=lf
*.yml                text eol=lf
*.yaml               text eol=lf
*.env                text eol=lf
go.mod               text eol=lf
go.sum               text eol=lf
Containerfile        text eol=lf

# Diagrams are rendered output.
rendered/*.svg       text eol=lf
